WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.030
Let’s say I’m running a giveaway.

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:04.070
I can put the Bitcoin aside

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.070
before I know who’ll win.

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:08.450
In this earlier test,

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:11.530
I funded a gift with 20,000 test sats.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:13.750
It has its own Bitcoin address.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:16.350
Once I have a winner,

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:17.680
I enter their NEAR account

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.120
and pass them the claim.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.150
I don’t need their Bitcoin address.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:24.750
Now they’re the holder.

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:26.970
They choose where to receive the Bitcoin,

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:28.750
and approve the payout.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.400
NEAR Chain Signatures authorizes it,

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.450
then the browser sends Bitcoin.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:38.550
This earlier test used a terminal wallet.

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:41.050
Here’s what the recipient sees today.

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:44.550
19,750 test sats delivered,

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:47.150
after a 250-sat fee.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.350
If they want to check,

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:52.500
the transaction is right here.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:53.900
Fund the prize first.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.150
Let the winner choose where it goes.
